            <ArticleTitle>Pregnancy and delivery in a patient with a Studer orthotopic ileal neobladder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>431-433</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5173/ceju.2016.877</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pregnancies in patients after cystectomy with urinary diversion, especially after the construction of a continent urinary reservoir, are rare. Experience in this field is limited and mainly concerns patients with congenital disorders, neurogenic diseases or trauma. In this paper, we report the outcome of pregnancy, delivery and the postpartum period in a 27-year old woman with a Studer ileal orthotopic neobladder after radical cystectomy, performed after the diagnosis of a malignant tumor at the age of 14.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
